<title>FRANCE: Michelin 1996 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Michelin 1996 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   2,892  vs	   2,796</p>
<p>    Net					    3,112  vs	   2,961</p>
<p>    Net excluding exceptionals	     3,957  vs	   2,889</p>
<p>    Operating				    6,956  vs	   5,698</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		 5,553  vs	   3,983</p>
<p>    Exceptional			 charges  845  vs     gain   72</p>
<p>    Financial expense			  1,403  vs	   1,715</p>
<p>    Tax on profit				1,355  vs	     984</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     8,357  vs	   4,358</p>
<p>    Turnover				    71,246  vs	  66,110</p>
<p>Dividends (francs)</p>
<p>     -- A shares				  3.40  vs	    2.85</p>
<p>-- B shares and partially amortised</p>
<p>	    A shares				3.30  vs	    2.75</p>
<p>NOTE - Compagnie Generale des Etablissements Michelin issued its results in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the dividend would be proposed at the annual general meeting on June 12 and would be payable in cash or B shares.</p>
<p>Operating profit in 1996 was around 10 percent of turnover.</p>
<p>Financial expense was two percent of turnover in 1996, compared with 2.6 percent in the preceding year, due to a 3.4 billion franc reduction in debt to 22.8 billion francs at the end of last year. The debt-to-equity ratio was thus reduced to 1.31 at December 31, 1996, from 2.02 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Michelin said 1996 exceptional items include restructuring charges and capital gains. It said in its 1996 first-half results that it took a 709 million franc charge for the restructuring of its Spanish subsidiary Neumaticos Michelin SA.</p>
<p>Investment was 3.3 billion francs in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
